.TH RPB 1 "2026-07-09" "reta arch mojo" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
rpb \- run one Reta prompt command and exit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rpb
.RI command ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rpb
is the one-shot Reta prompt frontend.  It builds a single prompt command from
its arguments, executes it and exits.  It is the right command for scripts,
smoke tests and shell pipelines that need prompt syntax without opening an
interactive session.
.PP
The profile uses vi-style historical defaults and applies the compact
.B e
behaviour by default.  Unlike
.BR rp ,
.B rpl
and
.BR rpe ,
.B rpb
does not load the interactive prompt-input library.  It uses the shared prompt
execution library and the Reta core library only.
.SH COMMANDS
.B rpb
accepts the same prompt command language as
.BR rp (1).
Common examples are
.BR prim ,
.BR multis ,
.BR modulo ,
.BR abc ,
.BR abstand ,
.BR abstandPrim ,
short table commands such as
.B a
or
.B u
and complete
.B reta
commands.
.SH OPTIONS
Because
.B rpb
is already a one-shot profile, its remaining arguments are normally interpreted
as the command.  For startup help use
.BR -h
or
.BR -help .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/rpb
Default public executable for a standard installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_mojo.so
Shared prompt execution library used by
.BR rpb .
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_core_mojo.so
Reta table core library reached by the prompt execution path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Prime factorisation:
.PP
.nf
rpb prim 60
.fi
.PP
Run a compact table command:
.PP
.nf
rpb a 2
.fi
.PP
Run a full Reta command through prompt syntax:
.PP
.nf
rpb reta -zeilen --vorhervonausschnitt=1-2 \\
        -spalten --religionen=sternpolygon --breite=40
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rp (1),
.BR rpl (1),
.BR rpe (1),
.BR reta (1)
